## 6. What we should lock before development

The mapping is now internally consistent: 90 lessons, five assigned question briefs per lesson, 15 dataset domains, and ten projects.

However, I would not freeze every dataset schema or question wording yet. We should first complete one end-to-end reference implementation using D01 Retail Commerce, including its source license, table relationships, sample fixtures, five questions for L008, reference solutions, and automated grading.

Once that passes, we can apply the same standard to the remaining datasets and question groups.

This gives runtime.school a single traceable curriculum blueprint: every planned question belongs to a lesson, every lesson has assigned data, and every project reuses the same dataset library.